  "notes": "South wins the opening heart lead and must avoid the loss of 4 trump tricks. If trumps are 3-2 there will be no problem. If West has 4 spades including the ♠A, ♠K, and ♠Q the contract will fail.\n\nThe other 4-1 trump breaks are the relevant cases. It seems natural for South to play a high spade at trick 2. South can later cross to the dummy and lead a spade towards the closed hand. This line of play will fail when East started with a singleton spade honour. There are 3 possible singleton spade honours (the ♠A, ♠K, and ♠Q) that East could have.\n\nSouth improves his chances slightly by leading a low spade out of the closed hand. This play will lose when West has a singleton small spade. Since there are only 2 singleton small spades (the ♠8 and ♠7) that West could have, this is a superior line of play.",
